This problem setup is to test the ability of ERF to correctly use files created
by the WRF Preprocessing System (WPS) to initialize the problem and provide
time-dependent boundary conditions.

The inputs_wps_ml_interp case covers the surface-only initialization path
(erf.interp_atmos_from_coarse, issue #4060): level 1 is created part-way
through the run from a wrfinput_d02 whose start time is later than
wrfinput_d01's, reading only the surface and SLM fields from the file and
interpolating the atmospheric state from level 0. It runs on the same
summer dataset as inputs_slm_rrtmgp (SLM requires the radiation model, and
its canopy scheme cannot run a below-freezing dataset) and needs: those
wrfinput_d01/wrfbdy_d01 files; a wrfinput_d02 with parent_grid_ratio = 3
and a start time 25 s after d01's; NoahmpTable.TBL; and the four
rrtmgp-*.nc files named in the inputs (see below). Build with
USE_RRTMGP=TRUE. Pick max_step so the run crosses the d02 start time.

The inputs_noahmp_rrtmgp case employs the Noah-MP land surface model
and RRTMGP radiation model. A namelist file, Noah-MP table file, and radiation data files
are needed for this case;
see `https://erf.readthedocs.io/en/latest/CouplingToNoahMP.html?highlight=namelist+erf`
(obtained with the `wget` command) and
`https://github.com/erf-model/data-files` (clone the repository).
The needed files must be copied into the current directory before running the simulation.
